## Phase 1: Contract And Context Foundation
<!-- phase: 1 -->
- [x] <!-- id: p1-contract-mode --> Package 1.1 ships additive mode handling and response-schema normalization without removing current top-level keys. | proof=Implemented runtime mode/result normalization in runtime.py + quality/results.py, preserved top-level keys, added additive metadata fields, and passed tests/test_manage_docs_quality_check.py (11 passed).
Proof: targeted tests on the `quality_check` response shape and a source readback showing no new public action.
Dependency: none.
- [x] <!-- id: p1-context-parser --> Package 1.2 ships `DocumentContext` plus a parser decision or fallback adapter that passes the fence and container regression corpus. | proof=Regression assertions now verify container behavior boundaries in tests/doc_management/test_quality_context.py: blockquote-contained fence text is not captured as fenced scope by current provider behavior, list-contained fenced block is captured, table rows and inline code are excluded from fenced scope, indented code is not treated as fenced scope and remains in body text, and unclosed fences are flagged. Verification: pytest -q tests/doc_management/test_quality_context.py (2 passed), pytest -q tests/test_manage_docs_quality_check.py (11 passed), pytest -q tests/test_manage_docs_scaffold_quality.py (18 passed), git diff --check clean.
Proof: context tests cover quadruple fences, tilde fences, blockquotes, lists, tables, inline code, indented code, and unclosed fences.
Dependency: `p1-contract-mode`.

## Phase 2: Core Rule Migration
<!-- phase: 2 -->
- [x] <!-- id: p2-registry --> Package 2.1 ships the deterministic registry while keeping `scaffold_quality.py` as the compatibility facade. | proof=Deterministic registry infrastructure exists in `src/scribe_mcp/doc_management/quality/registry.py` with stable ordering and activation predicates, with internal exports in `src/scribe_mcp/doc_management/quality/__init__.py`. `src/scribe_mcp/doc_management/scaffold_quality.py` remains the import-stable compatibility facade for `collect_managed_doc_quality_warnings` and `summarize_quality_warnings` without migrating production rule families in Package 2.1. Verification target: `pytest -q tests/doc_management/test_quality_registry.py`.
Proof: unit tests show stable registry ordering and existing helper imports still pass.
Dependency: `p1-contract-mode`, `p1-context-parser`.
- [x] <!-- id: p2-scaffold-rules --> Package 2.2 migrates scaffold and lifecycle rules onto scoped evaluation without changing existing warning IDs unexpectedly. | proof=SCF scaffold, lifecycle, trailing-whitespace, and readiness-conformance evaluation moved into `src/scribe_mcp/doc_management/quality/rules/scaffold.py` and is delegated from `scaffold_quality.py` while preserving warning IDs, blocking semantics, payload shape, and facade helpers. Regression tests in `tests/test_manage_docs_scaffold_quality.py` cover nested fenced placeholders, inline-code placeholder examples, indented-code placeholder examples, markdown table bracket text false-positive suppression, and authored placeholders still warning. Verification: scaffold_quality 22 passed, quality_registry 1 passed, quality_context 2 passed, quality_check 11 passed, git diff --check clean.
Proof: scaffold regression suite proves nested fences and table text no longer trigger false positives.
Dependency: `p2-registry`.
- [x] <!-- id: p2-research-rules --> Package 2.3 migrates research placement and index hygiene with explicit research-owner metadata. | proof=Research placement and index hygiene moved into `src/scribe_mcp/doc_management/quality/rules/research.py`; `SCF_NONCANONICAL_LOCATION`, `SCF_INDEX_MISSING`, `SCF_DOC_UNINDEXED`, and `SCF_INDEX_STALE` stay stable; direct research warnings carry `source_owner: research`; project_health warning digest compatibility is covered in tests. Verification: project_health_quality passed, scaffold_quality passed, quality_registry passed, quality_check passed, git diff --check clean.
Proof: research-doc checks still detect noncanonical placement and stale or missing index coverage.
Dependency: `p2-registry`.

## Phase 3: Changelog And Release Gating
<!-- phase: 3 -->
- [x] <!-- id: p3-changelog-structure --> Package 3.1 migrates changelog structure rules while preserving existing helper reuse. | proof=Moved structural changelog checks into `src/scribe_mcp/doc_management/quality/rules/changelog.py` while reusing `parse_changelog_entries`/`accepted_entries`; `scaffold_quality.py` remains compatibility facade; local_default no longer requires version/subprocess release inference for structure checks. Verification: test_changelog_quality 5 passed; manage_docs_scaffold_quality 22 passed; manage_docs_quality_check 11 passed; quality_registry 1 passed; git diff --check clean.
Proof: changelog tests still catch missing IDs, missing evidence, raw progress dumps, and escaped-newline sludge.
Dependency: `p2-registry`.
- [x] <!-- id: p3-release-gate --> Package 3.2 moves current-version coverage and research-context drift behind explicit or conservatively inferred `release_gate` semantics and finalizes suppressibility policy. | proof=Current-version coverage evaluator runs only when resolved runtime mode is `release_gate`, emitted as unsuppressible `SCF_CHANGELOG_CURRENT_VERSION_MISSING` in `collect_managed_doc_quality_warnings` for CHANGELOG. Explicit and inferred release-gate both emit/block when coverage is missing, while `local_default` remains non-blocking. Tests: `pytest -q tests/doc_management/test_quality_release_modes.py` (8 passed), `pytest -q tests/doc_management/test_research_context_drift.py` (4 passed), `pytest -q tests/doc_management/test_changelog_quality.py` (5 passed), `pytest -q tests/test_manage_docs_quality_check.py` (12 passed), `pytest -q tests/test_manage_docs_scaffold_quality.py` (22 passed), `pytest -q tests/doc_management/test_quality_registry.py` (1 passed).
Dependency: `p1-contract-mode`, `p2-registry`, `p3-changelog-structure`.

## Phase 4: Runtime Proof And Hardening
<!-- phase: 4 -->
- [x] <!-- id: p4-runtime-proof --> Package 4.1 proves alias routing, explicit markdown-path resolution, additive output stability, and the final profiling decision on caching. | proof=Added alias-route equivalence + cross-route legacy-key stability assertions in tests/test_manage_docs_quality_check.py; explicit markdown-path behavior remains proven by repo-relative and absolute-path tests. Verification passed: `pytest -q tests/test_manage_docs_quality_check.py` (14 passed), `pytest -q tests/doc_management/test_quality_release_modes.py` (8 passed), `pytest -q tests/test_manage_docs_scaffold_quality.py` (22 passed), `pytest -q tests/doc_management/test_quality_registry.py` (1 passed), `git diff --check` clean. Runtime profile (uv run, 25 iterations each): `quality_check avg_ms=1.760 p95_ms=1.083`; `scaffold_quality_check avg_ms=0.925 p95_ms=1.001`; decision: no caching justified.
Proof: Alias and scaffold routes return equivalent payloads, markdown-path resolution works within project-root constraints, legacy top-level response keys remain present, and profiling indicates local_default latency is already acceptably fast without cache complexity.
Dependency: all prior phase packages.

